+// Triggers bypass ActionRunner: TriggerRunner (src/triggers/trigger-runner.ts) resolves the connection itself and
+// reaches the provider through the connection's proxy executor. The rule on a read-only connection:
+//   - refused: `reconcile` (creates or deletes a webhook) and `resource` (subscribes or unsubscribes a resource);
+//   - allowed: `read` (polling), `options`, `receive` (verifies an inbound delivery) and `source` (local identity
+//     and signature checks), because none of them changes anything on the provider;
+//   - allowed: cleanup of an existing subscription (admin cancel route and the maintenance job), because removing
+//     a webhook SplitMind itself created is housekeeping, not a caller's write.
